WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.501
Nikhil: From calorie
down to portion sizes,

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.936
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:05.605
between Lay's chips in
the US and in India.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.273
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.712
Here are all the Lay's
chips you'll find in India

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.748
that you won't find in the US.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.683
And here are all the Lay's chips in the US

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.018
you can't find in India.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:21.354
Oh, my good God. Yeah!

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.423
To begin things, I'm
going to go with the one

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:26.526
I hate the most, Spanish tomato tango.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.528
Yeah, I just never
really liked this flavor.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.530
It's just too heavy on the tomato side.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:36.403
No. Oh, man, that aftertaste is horrible.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.371
I have nothing nice to
say about this flavor.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.340
Also, just to note, our
standard Lay's chips

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.841
come in the ridge style.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.110
We do also sell the flat style,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.312
but that's more of a
special variety of Lay's.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.382
Next, it's West Indies
hot and sweet chili,

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.851
formerly Caribbean hot and sweet chili.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.355
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.322
Get out of here!

00:00:56.322 --> 00:01:00.126
And now for the maharaja of Indian Lay's,

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.095
magic masala.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.430
If you haven't heard of this,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.697
you must be living under a rock,

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.667
because this is the
little emperor of chips.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.403
Commonly known as blue Lay's.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.406
Look at this chip, dude!

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.707
Oh, my God.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.211
Oh, my God.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.381
It's already so spicy.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:24.217
The reason this chip has
become so popular in India

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.519
is because they have
actually managed to capture

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.822
the masala of India so well.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.924
And masala, if you're wondering,
is, like, ground-up spices

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:34.828
that are added to every
single dish we eat here.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.496
This is truly magic.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.498
I want to know what they're like.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.799
Joe got himself something.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:41.701
Oh, man.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:45.939
And the chip bags in India
are, like, much harder to open.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.174
Oh, man! You guys got
them locked up tight.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.511
Got a rip! OK.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.812
Yeah.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.347
Oh, yeah.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.182
Damn, these are good!

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.684
Not too spicy.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.985
Great flavor.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.653
We have so many flavors.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.255
I couldn't get them all for this shoot.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.023
I mean, I'll just start right here.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.227
Barbecue. This is the classic chip.

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:09.362
I think this is more popular
than the classic, to be honest.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.064
The US has, I would say,

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.933
at least 10 different variations
of barbecue, possibly more.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.735
So to have just, like,
standard barbecue is

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.104
pretty bold move by Lay's.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.472
Salt and vinegar.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.474
[dreamy harp tune]

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.542
Love salt and vinegar so much.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.444
I love it so much.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.613
Top chip. Top chip right here.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:27.847
Love salt and vinegar.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.048
Cheddar and sour cream.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.384
Ha ha ha, limón.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.753
Another favorite. Oh, man.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:37.323
It seems like lime-flavored
chips would be weird,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.825
or citrusy chips, but ...

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:40.860
so good.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.929
And these are, like, really limey.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.932
All the superfans watching
know I do not like pickles.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.136
No.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.471
Let's kick it up a notch.

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:52.939
Flamin' Hot dill pickle.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.307
And the Flamin' Hot, that font,

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.910
that implies that's
Flamin' Hot Cheetos, right?

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.980
Mm. Better.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.482
Still not that good.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.851
Last in this group is a chili limón.

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:06.953
Yeah.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.722
These are coming home with me.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.124
Other flavors in this category

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.725
that I couldn't get at
the time of filming,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:16.396
cheddar jalapeño and sweet
Southern heat barbecue.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.097
I was totally able to buy them online.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.966
I get a thing in the mail two days ago

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.702
saying the post office
is holding them ransom

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:25.438
and wants 5 more dollars for
postage for me to pick it up.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:26.439
Not happening.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.275
I will not be intimidated by
the United States post office.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.376
You keep the chips, all right?

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.811
Also what I couldn't get
at the time of filming

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:35.481
was honey barbecue,
Chesapeake Bay crab spice,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.384
adobadas, which is a different spicy chip

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.219
which is actually very good.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.453
I was bummed I couldn't get those.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:44.157
And the Doritos Cool Ranch
Lay's, unfortunately.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.059
Let's now talk about two exclusive flavors

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.695
that are in both countries,
but slightly different.

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.397
We have the sizzlin' hot Lay's

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:54.200
and the American-style cream and onion.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.337
It was previously known as
American sour cream and onion.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.474
It's great. No fuss.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.042
One of my favorite flavors.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.311
It's been there for, like,
over two decades, I feel,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.880
in India, and there's a reason for that.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.049
Ours is just regular sour cream and onion.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:13.119
And I also got American-style
sour cream and onion

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.087
from India.

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.189
And then,

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.523
one after the other.

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.861
The flavor on these are much stronger.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:24.030
And it even says, "Now with more flavor."

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.265
This is more flavor?

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:27.533
I gotta say, I like
these India ones better.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.235
Up next, we have sizzlin' hot.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.504
This is a flavor I've actually never had.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.006
I'm very excited to see how it stacks

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:36.442
compared to magic masala,
which is already pretty spicy.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.811
Whoa.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.780
Yo, look at this chip.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:41.948
It's literally red.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.019
Not really -- oh.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.721
Nice.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.958
It's not as much a direct
heat as the magic masala.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.259
Hey, this is a nice flavor.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:56.329
In the US, we have Flamin' Hot flavor.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:57.163
Now, let me explain.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.765
This is Flamin' Hot kettle chips.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.366
Couldn't get the regular Flamin' Hot.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.035
We'll get into kettle chips later.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:04.003
It's, like, regular spice.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.838
It has a heat to it
without being too specific.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.574
I think they use these
red chilies right here.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:09.575
It packs a nice punch

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.577
without being too
overwhelming with the flavor.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:12.745
They're, like, the perfect amount of heat

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.314
without getting too overwhelming, so.

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.316
OK, so we don't only
have ridge-style chips,

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.717
we also have some flat ones.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.585
In fact, they're called wafer style,

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:22.388
which I think is pretty much
your classic style of Lay's.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:25.491
The first flavor is salt with pepper.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.160
Not salt and pepper.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.594
Don't you dare say that.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.499
It's very nice. I should
buy these more often.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.702
I've never tried these
before. Very good job.

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:37.770
OK, on to the next wafer-style chip.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.039
We have sun-dried chili.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:43.209
Mm! I love sun-dried anything.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:47.714
Beam that sun ray onto any
vegetable. I will eat it.

00:05:48.715 --> 00:05:50.516
Oh, damn.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.219
This is really good.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.721
They smashed it with this one.

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.490
Got a proper kick as well.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.558
Ooh!

00:05:58.558 --> 00:05:59.525
It's really yum.

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.495
And one of the most beautiful
sights you'll see in India

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:05.965
is people sun-drying their
own chilies on their roofs,

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.467
porches, wherever.

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:10.703
Biryanis, curries, they
all use sun-dried chili.

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:13.339
And this chip's packet really
has nailed this flavor.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.275
Maybe my favorite, kettle cooked.

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:19.312
We already saw the
Flamin' Hot kettle cooked.

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:20.880
These are thicker chip.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.482
They transport a lot better, obviously.

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.217
There are not as many broken.

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:26.753
It's got more of, like, a potato
taste to it, a potato snap.

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:27.920
It's like ...

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.988
I love kettle chips.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.957
Sea salt, cracked pepper.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:34.160
These are so good.

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:38.264
Mm. Yeah!

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:39.966
It's like ...

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:40.800
booyah!

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.535
[grunts]

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.270
Sea salt and vinegar.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.239
This ain't your pond salt.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.007
This ain't your lake salt.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.443
This certainly is not your fjord salt.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.013
Why is salt and vinegar so good?

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:55.014
Attention, everyone,

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.984
my favorite kettle chip is
about to be eaten by me.

00:06:57.984 --> 00:06:59.519
The jalapeño kettle chips.

00:06:59.519 --> 00:07:01.354
I'm not going to talk about Miss Vickie's

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:02.822
because this isn't a Miss Vickie's video.

00:07:02.822 --> 00:07:04.657
And I hate to say it.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:05.725
These might be better.

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.729
They've got the jalapeño flavor in there.

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:10.863
It's not too spicy,

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.398
so you can really chow down on these.

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:14.367
Moving on, unfortunately,

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:17.003
to something that I kind of can't stand,

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:19.972
are baked. Wah-wah.

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.107
You can get them in original

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.575
and you can get them in barbecue.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.212
Like eating cardboard.

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:29.849
Lay's has something called
the Better for You series.

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:32.351
So we have these, and then
lightly salted barbecue,

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.120
lightly salted wavy.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.757
I mean, I want the salt,
but, like, how much ... ?

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:39.225
This is what paper tastes like.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:42.462
We got simply sea salt thick cut.

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:45.531
And you can also get the
simply barbecue thick cut.

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:48.234
They have something called
layers, which are these guys.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:51.938
Bite-size layers, crispy
layers, tasty layers.

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:55.408
You can get them in three
cheese, sour cream and onion.

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.477
I've never seen these
before in my entire life.

00:07:57.477 --> 00:07:59.111
Oh, the bag stinks!

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.515
Oh, these are really bad.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.516
These are terrible.

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:05.251
Whoa, these are real chemically tasting.

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:07.220
Oh, my God, these taste
like they were poisoned.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.622
And now for our next
range of exclusive chips,

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:12.925
we have Lay's Maxx.

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.228
That's Maxx with two X's.

00:08:15.228 --> 00:08:18.164
Why the two X's? That's like
saying it's more better.

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.833
I have not seen or tasted these before.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.135
Starting with macho chili flavor.

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:26.606
It is kind of ridged, but
I would say it's more wavy.

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:29.542
I wouldn't say it's super spicy.

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:31.744
I kind of like that this one doesn't leave

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:33.813
that burning sensation in your throat.

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.414
It's really nice.

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.016
Yeah. I don't know about the branding,

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.718
but I really like this flavor.

00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:40.686
Next flavor, peppery cheddar.

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.993
Whoa. All sorts of stuff happening here.

00:08:46.993 --> 00:08:48.794
There's, like, some mint to it.

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:50.796
Oh, you know what this tastes like?

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:54.233
This tastes like malai tikka,
like chicken malai tikka

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:56.702
dipped in pudina chutney.

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.538
This is very unique.

00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:02.608
Our next flavor is sizzling barbecue.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:06.178
Oh, the reason this is called Lay's Maxx,

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:10.082
it's because it has
max crunch, max flavor,

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:11.250
and max taste.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:15.087
And I can wholeheartedly say
both of these have delivered.

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:21.661
Mm. It even smells
strongly of barbecue, so.

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:22.929
These work. They're great.

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:26.499
More fun chip styles.

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:29.602
I think we can call these the India style,

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:31.771
but we also call them the wavy style.

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:33.906
They are wavy, hence the name.

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:36.742
And you can get them in
original, reduced fat,

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:39.111
honey barbecue, ranch,

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:41.080
and you can also get
them in salt and pepper,

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.548
lightly salted,

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:45.151
fat, low fat, if I
didn't say that already.

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:46.852
The waves are, like, wider.

00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:49.956
You guys have, like,
really condensed waves.

00:09:49.956 --> 00:09:52.925
Lay's apparently wanted to
answer the age-old question,

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:54.894
how can we copy something popular

00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:57.697
and make it much, much worse?

00:09:57.697 --> 00:09:59.365
And Stax were invented.

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:00.733
You guys know what Pringles are, right?

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:02.001
Of course you do. Well.

00:10:02.001 --> 00:10:04.737
[chip pieces rattling] Hear that?

00:10:04.737 --> 00:10:06.272
"We'll put them in a tube.
They won't break as easily."

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.174
Right? [chip pieces rattling]

00:10:08.174 --> 00:10:10.543
Holy f---.

00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:11.677
Look at this.

00:10:15.181 --> 00:10:16.816
Then what was the point of
putting it in this tube?

00:10:16.816 --> 00:10:18.417
I hate this so much.

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:20.853
But to really prove my point,

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:22.421
yo, dog, look what I got.

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:26.325
By the way, paper too. Excellent idea,

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:28.127
Dave Pringle, whatever your name is.

00:10:35.134 --> 00:10:36.335
F--- Stax.

00:10:36.335 --> 00:10:38.904
And now to our final set of exclusives,

00:10:38.904 --> 00:10:41.007
the gourmet collection.

00:10:41.007 --> 00:10:43.442
I've had a lot of gourmet food in my life,

00:10:43.442 --> 00:10:47.580
and I've very rarely been
actually impressed with the food.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:50.116
Vintage cheese and paprika!

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.653
Vintage cheese and paprika.

00:10:55.054 --> 00:10:56.255
Oh.

00:10:56.255 --> 00:10:57.623
If I had tasted this chip

00:10:57.623 --> 00:10:59.659
without any of the fancy packaging,

00:10:59.659 --> 00:11:01.460
I don't think gourmet is the first word

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:02.595
that would come to my head.

00:11:02.595 --> 00:11:04.363
Thai sweet chili gourmet.

00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:10.736
This literally tastes like
the West Indies hot and chili,

00:11:10.736 --> 00:11:11.737
but on a flat chip.

00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:13.806
So gourmet is just packaging.

00:11:13.806 --> 00:11:15.307
That's what we've learned
from this experiment

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:17.076
with these two chips.

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:18.310
Skippable.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:21.113
In addition to that, we
also have Lay's Poppables.

00:11:21.113 --> 00:11:23.449
Poppables come in sea salt and vinegar --

00:11:23.449 --> 00:11:26.652
oh, Julius Pringle! That
was his name. Not Dave.

00:11:26.652 --> 00:11:29.555
They also have Poppables
sea salt and vinegar,

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:31.891
Poppables sea salt,
Poppable white cheddar,

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:33.693
and Poppable honey barbecue.

00:11:33.693 --> 00:11:35.161
OK, I don't want to eat all these.

00:11:35.161 --> 00:11:37.263
What's the cereal that looks like this?

00:11:37.263 --> 00:11:38.330
Is it Chex?

00:11:40.733 --> 00:11:42.668
If you got these on accident, eat them,

00:11:42.668 --> 00:11:45.971
but I wouldn't reach for these
over regular potato chips.

00:11:48.007 --> 00:11:51.210
Here in India, our Lay's chips
packets come in five sizes.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.546
There's 30 grams, 50 grams,

00:11:53.546 --> 00:11:55.948
73 grams, 104 grams,

00:11:55.948 --> 00:11:58.451
and 174 grams.

00:11:58.451 --> 00:12:00.553
The big boy. The party pack.

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:02.321
I feel like I could eat
this whole thing on my own,

00:12:02.321 --> 00:12:03.389
to be honest.

00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:07.727
In the US, our Lay's chips
come in six variety of sizes.

00:12:07.727 --> 00:12:10.029
All the way down here, got a 28-gram bag,

00:12:10.029 --> 00:12:11.597
which comes in the multipack.

00:12:11.597 --> 00:12:14.333
Next up, 74.4-gram bag.

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:18.003
In the middle here, there's
also an elusive 78-gram bag.

00:12:18.003 --> 00:12:21.774
Look, I saw it on Target.com
and Walmart.com. It exists.

00:12:21.774 --> 00:12:24.677
It just wasn't available
anywhere in Southern California.

00:12:24.677 --> 00:12:25.745
I looked, OK?

00:12:25.745 --> 00:12:27.279
One step up, we have what I think

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:30.549
is the classic grocery-store bag,

00:12:30.549 --> 00:12:35.054
226 gram, aka the 8-ounce bag.

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:36.689
You've seen it a million
times. This is the one.

00:12:36.689 --> 00:12:39.625
Right next to that one
is the family-sized bag,

00:12:39.625 --> 00:12:41.260
which I also couldn't get ahold of.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.629
297.6-gram bag.

00:12:43.629 --> 00:12:46.766
I couldn't find it because
the American family is dead.

00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:49.335
But what is alive and well is,
of course, our biggest size,

00:12:49.335 --> 00:12:53.439
the party size, 368 grams.

00:12:53.439 --> 00:12:57.309
All you family-less partyers,
Lay's has you covered.

00:12:57.309 --> 00:13:00.112
That means that the biggest bag in the US

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:03.716
is this much larger than
the biggest bag in India.

00:13:03.716 --> 00:13:05.518
But wait, there's more,

00:13:05.518 --> 00:13:07.787
or less, depending on
the packet that you get,

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:09.054
because according to Amazon,

00:13:09.054 --> 00:13:11.791
the weights of these
different packets might vary.

00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:13.726
So they're given a weight range.

00:13:13.726 --> 00:13:15.928
The biggest weight difference
is in our largest pack

00:13:15.928 --> 00:13:20.399
of 174 to 190 grams, which
is a difference of 16 grams.

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:22.701
So let's see how much
we get in one packet.

00:13:22.701 --> 00:13:25.371
Ooh!

00:13:25.371 --> 00:13:29.909
175 grams, one gram extra
from what is advertised,

00:13:29.909 --> 00:13:31.076
which is, I'll take it.

00:13:31.076 --> 00:13:33.579
So let me show you what 16
grams of chips looks like,

00:13:33.579 --> 00:13:35.948
so you can see what you're
potentially missing out on.

00:13:35.948 --> 00:13:38.050
It doesn't seem like a
lot, but I think that's

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:40.219
quite a substantial amount of
chips you're missing out on.

00:13:40.219 --> 00:13:44.957
To be fair, they did write
174 grams only on the pack.

00:13:44.957 --> 00:13:47.960
In the US, our flavor bags weigh less

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.562
than the original-flavor bag.

00:13:49.562 --> 00:13:52.998
Take this barbecue-flavored Lay's bag.

00:13:52.998 --> 00:13:57.803
It weighs 7.75 ounces, or 7 ¾ ounces.

00:13:57.803 --> 00:13:59.505
Yuelei, can we get in there?

00:13:59.505 --> 00:14:00.606
You see that? Thank you.

00:14:00.606 --> 00:14:03.776
Compared to the 8 ounce you
get with the original bag.

00:14:03.776 --> 00:14:06.745
OK. Same price, less product.

00:14:06.745 --> 00:14:08.781
Now, Harry did research on that episode,

00:14:08.781 --> 00:14:10.749
so take it away, Harry.

00:14:10.749 --> 00:14:12.518
What? No, do your own research.

00:14:12.518 --> 00:14:14.787
According to Harry's research
from the last Lay's episode,

00:14:14.787 --> 00:14:18.224
back in 2014, PepsiCo claimed
the reason that there is

00:14:18.224 --> 00:14:21.594
a slightly higher price per
ounce for flavored chips

00:14:21.594 --> 00:14:22.895
is the added seasoning.

00:14:22.895 --> 00:14:25.464
So then, Lay's,

00:14:25.464 --> 00:14:28.667
can you explain to me why
this lightly salted bag

00:14:28.667 --> 00:14:30.669
gives you fewer chips
than the original bag?

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:33.572
It's more money but less salt, eh, Lay's?

00:14:33.572 --> 00:14:34.740
Check it out.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:38.344
The lightly salted, so
less salted than this,

00:14:38.344 --> 00:14:39.979
also 7 ¾.

00:14:39.979 --> 00:14:42.381
While we're exposing potential Lay's lies,

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:45.084
this 28-gram bag in the US

00:14:45.084 --> 00:14:49.255
supposedly contains 15 chips,
according to Lay's website.

00:14:49.255 --> 00:14:51.357
Let's see how accurate this is.

00:14:51.357 --> 00:14:53.559
And I'm going to count all the
chips in this 30-gram packet

00:14:53.559 --> 00:14:54.827
to see how many we have.

00:14:57.563 --> 00:15:00.332
I mean, it doesn't contain one whole chip.

00:15:01.467 --> 00:15:02.801
One.

00:15:02.801 --> 00:15:05.905
12, 13.

00:15:05.905 --> 00:15:09.708
I mean, if we're doing it
by chip-related piles ...

00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:10.943
six, 12, eight?

00:15:10.943 --> 00:15:12.912
Close to 18 chips per bag.

00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:15.281
Huh. All right, I'll concede.

00:15:15.281 --> 00:15:17.216
Cool, so that's 24 chips.

00:15:17.216 --> 00:15:19.952
I would say, realistically,
this is, like, 20 chips

00:15:19.952 --> 00:15:22.087
that have been broken
into many other pieces.

00:15:22.087 --> 00:15:24.423
But let's be real, they
could've fit a lot more chips

00:15:24.423 --> 00:15:25.424
into this packet.

00:15:25.424 --> 00:15:28.494
And Lay's is notorious
for filling it with air.

00:15:28.494 --> 00:15:29.895
It's actually nitrogen gas,

00:15:29.895 --> 00:15:32.364
which helps preserve the chips
and also acts as a cushion

00:15:32.364 --> 00:15:34.366
to stop them from getting
smashed in transit.

00:15:34.366 --> 00:15:35.200
I mean ...

00:15:36.368 --> 00:15:38.170
What would it have been
like without the cushion?

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:40.139
This whole bag would've
been dust, apparently.

00:15:40.139 --> 00:15:42.908
But what is the
air-to-chip ratio, you ask?

00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:45.044
Let's find out in a new
segment I like to call

00:15:45.044 --> 00:15:47.279
the Ar-chip-medes principle.

00:15:51.083 --> 00:15:53.585
Can I just say, this is
one of the weirdest things

00:15:53.585 --> 00:15:54.753
I've done in my life.

00:15:54.753 --> 00:15:58.157
A generous 55 ml of chips in this packet.

00:15:58.157 --> 00:16:00.859
Now let's measure how
much the packet itself

00:16:00.859 --> 00:16:02.828
can hold in volume.

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:05.230
Score!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:07.132
Ooh, this smells so bad.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.234
900 ml.

00:16:09.234 --> 00:16:12.805
That's 845 ml of chips

00:16:12.805 --> 00:16:14.707
that we could have had, Lay's.

00:16:14.707 --> 00:16:16.008
I feel cheated.

00:16:16.008 --> 00:16:18.711
I think to make it more
accurate, let's do four.

00:16:18.711 --> 00:16:20.012
And then we'll fill this guy up,

00:16:20.012 --> 00:16:21.113
and then we'll divide by four,

00:16:21.113 --> 00:16:22.281
and that would give us
the average of those.

00:16:22.281 --> 00:16:23.315
Does that make sense?

00:16:23.315 --> 00:16:24.149
Dust.

00:16:26.352 --> 00:16:28.587
Uh-huh, all right.

00:16:28.587 --> 00:16:30.122
Oh, man. All right.

00:16:30.122 --> 00:16:34.593
Can I please have the scientific
chip-crunching nunchucks?

00:16:34.593 --> 00:16:35.828
Throw them!

00:16:35.828 --> 00:16:38.597
Ah! Whoa!

00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:39.431
Look out, chips.

00:16:39.431 --> 00:16:41.867
Pow. Pow. Pow.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:48.607
2.75 fluid ounces per bag.

00:16:48.607 --> 00:16:51.610
Now that's science you can use.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:54.179
So, now we're going to
fill this with water.

00:16:54.179 --> 00:16:55.014
Ugh.

00:16:55.014 --> 00:16:58.717
The whole thing's 20, which is about 2.75.

00:16:58.717 --> 00:17:02.888
17.25 units of whatever.

00:17:02.888 --> 00:17:04.656
Cubic fluid ounces?

00:17:04.656 --> 00:17:06.658
Even more interesting air information.

00:17:06.658 --> 00:17:09.128
Because of India's varied geography,

00:17:09.128 --> 00:17:11.263
the amount of air that's
packed into these packets

00:17:11.263 --> 00:17:13.432
is different for different altitudes.

00:17:13.432 --> 00:17:15.601
For example, in cities of higher altitude,

00:17:15.601 --> 00:17:17.403
like Leh in the Himalayas,

00:17:17.403 --> 00:17:20.906
there is the risk of
these packets exploding

00:17:20.906 --> 00:17:22.875
due to the low atmospheric pressure.

00:17:22.875 --> 00:17:24.176
And so, when they're sent there,

00:17:24.176 --> 00:17:27.279
they're sent with no air
at all inside of them.

00:17:27.279 --> 00:17:30.282
And so they run the risk of
being crushed in transport,

00:17:30.282 --> 00:17:34.319
so they have to be taken as
delicately as a crate of eggs.

00:17:36.622 --> 00:17:38.524
But what about price?

00:17:38.524 --> 00:17:41.794
This is our largest chips
packet, the 174 grams.

00:17:41.794 --> 00:17:45.798
And on Swiggy and Amazon, this
sells for about 78 rupees,

00:17:45.798 --> 00:17:47.800
which is about a dollar right now.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:50.035
And that equals ...

00:17:51.804 --> 00:17:55.174
rupees 0.44 per gram.

00:17:55.174 --> 00:17:57.709
About $0.005.

00:17:57.709 --> 00:18:01.013
And, yes, I did all of that
math and conversion in my head.

00:18:01.013 --> 00:18:02.514
Here in the US, if we break it down

00:18:02.514 --> 00:18:03.682
starting with this big bag,

00:18:03.682 --> 00:18:07.686
the 226.8 gram, aka 8-ounce, bag,

00:18:07.686 --> 00:18:10.222
it's $3.99 at Target,

00:18:10.222 --> 00:18:13.258
or 316.58 rupees.

00:18:13.258 --> 00:18:14.760
Yes, it's a bigger bag, I know.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:18.263
So breaking it down per gram,
we found that in the US,

00:18:18.263 --> 00:18:22.434
the cost is a 260%
increase compared to India.

00:18:22.434 --> 00:18:23.902
While we do enjoy our Lay's chips,

00:18:23.902 --> 00:18:28.240
we also have a giant chip
culture here in India.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.275
In fact, these are called hot chips,

00:18:30.275 --> 00:18:32.010
and they're sold all across India

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:34.813
at stalls called hot-chip stalls,

00:18:34.813 --> 00:18:37.349
where, basically, they
have a giant frying pan,

00:18:37.349 --> 00:18:39.384
and they cut the potato in front of you

00:18:39.384 --> 00:18:41.353
to these thin slices and fry it

00:18:41.353 --> 00:18:43.889
and give it to you nice,
hot-hot, fresh-fresh.

00:18:43.889 --> 00:18:46.525
And so, for 174 grams,
which is the same as this,

00:18:46.525 --> 00:18:50.562
you're paying rupees 45
for a lot fresher chips.

00:18:50.562 --> 00:18:52.464
So as you can see, Lay's
is competing against

00:18:52.464 --> 00:18:55.000
a giant chip market here in India

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.236
and doing pretty well, I would say.

00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:01.240
Now for the burning question.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.375
Are there any questionable ingredients

00:19:03.375 --> 00:19:06.178
that are in your Lay's chips
that you need to watch out for?

00:19:06.178 --> 00:19:09.548
Fret not, because Joe and I
have found them out for you.

00:19:09.548 --> 00:19:12.351
As far as the basic salted version goes,

00:19:12.351 --> 00:19:13.185
you're totally fine.

00:19:13.185 --> 00:19:16.488
Both in India and the US,
they're made of potatoes,

00:19:16.488 --> 00:19:18.090
vegetable oil, salt.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.025
Warning! Warning alert!

00:19:20.025 --> 00:19:21.160
Here in India, some of our flavors

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:23.395
have an ingredient called
potassium chloride.

00:19:23.395 --> 00:19:25.397
In regular doses, this is completely safe,

00:19:25.397 --> 00:19:27.833
and it's a low-sodium alternative to salt.

00:19:27.833 --> 00:19:30.736
However, it's also one of
the three ingredients used

00:19:30.736 --> 00:19:35.641
in the three-drug cocktail
for lethal injections.

00:19:35.641 --> 00:19:39.478
Too much potassium chloride
will cause irregular heartbeats,

00:19:39.478 --> 00:19:41.079
and, boom, your heart will stop.

00:19:41.079 --> 00:19:44.616
So if you've been thinking
of doing a Lay's mukbang,

00:19:44.616 --> 00:19:45.817
be careful.

00:19:45.817 --> 00:19:47.486
We don't have any of that in the US Lay's,

00:19:47.486 --> 00:19:49.188
but we do have food coloring,

00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:54.026
caramel color in our barbecue
and honey-barbecue chips.

00:19:54.026 --> 00:19:56.161
Certain types of caramel
color can contain a byproduct

00:19:56.161 --> 00:19:59.798
called 4-meI.

00:19:59.798 --> 00:20:02.501
Studies found that it caused
cancer in rats and mice,

00:20:02.501 --> 00:20:06.004
leading campaigns in support
of banning it from foods.

00:20:06.004 --> 00:20:07.706
Give me that dancing rat!

00:20:08.941 --> 00:20:11.410
All right. The FDA was
like, "Meh, it's fine.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.712
Humans don't come close
to the level of exposure

00:20:13.712 --> 00:20:15.247
that caused the rat tumors."

00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:17.649
But that didn't stop
the state of California

00:20:17.649 --> 00:20:20.986
adding it to its Proposition
65 list of chemicals, quote,

00:20:20.986 --> 00:20:24.456
"known to the state of
California to cause cancer

00:20:24.456 --> 00:20:27.759
or reproductive toxicity," end quote. Oof.

00:20:27.759 --> 00:20:29.661
Another ingredient found
in several varieties

00:20:29.661 --> 00:20:32.965
of Lay's chips here in
India is disodium glutamate,

00:20:32.965 --> 00:20:36.568
aka flavor enhancer 69.

00:20:36.568 --> 00:20:38.637
No, not 69.

00:20:38.637 --> 00:20:41.106
Flavor enhancer 627.

00:20:41.106 --> 00:20:43.809
But basically, it's used alongside MSG

00:20:43.809 --> 00:20:46.345
to enhance the flavor of the chips.

00:20:46.345 --> 00:20:48.046
Both the Food and Drug Administration,

00:20:48.046 --> 00:20:49.715
or the FDA, in the United States,

00:20:49.715 --> 00:20:53.085
and the European Food Safety
Authority, or the EFSA,

00:20:53.085 --> 00:20:55.787
consider disodium glutamate safe.

00:20:55.787 --> 00:20:58.290
But it's not recommended
for babies, children,

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:00.058
pregnant women, and lactating mothers,

00:21:00.058 --> 00:21:02.127
and also should be avoided by asthmatics

00:21:02.127 --> 00:21:04.162
or people suffering from gout.

00:21:04.162 --> 00:21:04.997
MSG, if you're wondering,

00:21:04.997 --> 00:21:07.332
is the commonly misunderstood ingredient

00:21:07.332 --> 00:21:09.001
known as monosodium glutamate

00:21:09.001 --> 00:21:10.669
which is added to a lot of Asian cuisine

00:21:10.669 --> 00:21:13.038
and gives it that umami flavor.

00:21:13.038 --> 00:21:16.275
In 2019, Lay's sued a
bunch of Indian farmers

00:21:16.275 --> 00:21:20.412
for growing a certain variety
of potato, FC5 variety,

00:21:20.412 --> 00:21:23.649
saying it has a patent on that variety.

00:21:23.649 --> 00:21:25.951
This type of potato is
ideal for snack chips,

00:21:25.951 --> 00:21:28.453
as it has a lower moisture content.

00:21:28.453 --> 00:21:30.522
But strike one up for the little guy.

00:21:30.522 --> 00:21:32.424
Farmers'-rights activists
petitioned to the

00:21:32.424 --> 00:21:36.028
Protection of Plant Varieties
and Farmers' Rights Authority,

00:21:36.028 --> 00:21:37.029
and it agreed.

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:41.667
PepsiCo, Lay's, cannot claim
a patent over a seed variety.

00:21:41.667 --> 00:21:43.101
It was revoked immediately,

00:21:43.101 --> 00:21:45.437
and the Indian potato
farmers are now flush

00:21:45.437 --> 00:21:47.939
with low-moisture-potato money.

00:21:47.939 --> 00:21:50.475
Let's go!

00:21:52.978 --> 00:21:55.380
So, which country has
the unhealthiest chips?

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:57.582
Let's compare the classics first.

00:21:57.582 --> 00:22:00.919
A 28-gram bag of classic Lay's in the US

00:22:00.919 --> 00:22:04.790
contains 160 calories,
10 grams of total fat,

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:07.959
1.5 grams of saturated
fat, 15 grams of carbs,

00:22:07.959 --> 00:22:10.429
and 170 milligrams of sodium.

00:22:10.429 --> 00:22:13.098
OK, so our Lay's nutrition
is per 100 grams.

00:22:13.098 --> 00:22:14.299
So I did a little bit of math

00:22:14.299 --> 00:22:16.535
to compare it to the US 28 grams.

00:22:16.535 --> 00:22:17.502
Actually, Joe did the math.

00:22:17.502 --> 00:22:19.237
So if the math is wrong, blame Joe.

00:22:19.237 --> 00:22:22.174
OK, so we have 154.8 calories,

00:22:22.174 --> 00:22:24.009
total fat, 9.8 grams,

00:22:24.009 --> 00:22:26.778
of which saturates are 3.7 grams,

00:22:26.778 --> 00:22:28.380
carbs are 14.7 grams,

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:31.883
and sodium, 142.8 milligrams.

00:22:31.883 --> 00:22:33.552
Wow, that was pretty close, actually.

00:22:33.552 --> 00:22:35.153
We're under the US in every metric

00:22:35.153 --> 00:22:39.791
except for saturated fats,
where we are over 164%.

00:22:39.791 --> 00:22:42.427
And I think that's because
we use palm-olein oil

00:22:42.427 --> 00:22:45.731
to fry our chips, and it's
very high in saturated fats,

00:22:45.731 --> 00:22:48.266
unlike the US vegetable oil.

00:22:48.266 --> 00:22:50.969
What about the least-healthiest
chip in each country?

00:22:50.969 --> 00:22:52.971
Over here, there are a lot of them

00:22:52.971 --> 00:22:57.075
that are tied to 160
calories per 28-gram bag.

00:22:57.075 --> 00:22:58.710
Show list.

00:22:58.710 --> 00:23:01.913
But we did find that the 160-calorie chips

00:23:01.913 --> 00:23:04.449
with the highest fat content are these.

00:23:04.449 --> 00:23:05.951
No!

00:23:05.951 --> 00:23:08.620
The cheddar and sour
cream, I love these guys.

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:11.223
Making them the least healthy.

00:23:11.223 --> 00:23:13.091
If I did have a bag that small,

00:23:13.091 --> 00:23:15.694
it would contain all of this.

00:23:15.694 --> 00:23:19.264
And here in India, our
highest-calorific chip is

00:23:19.264 --> 00:23:20.665
classic salted.

00:23:20.665 --> 00:23:21.500
How lame.

00:23:21.500 --> 00:23:24.536
How is this the most calorific
chip we sell here, Lay's?

00:23:24.536 --> 00:23:25.771
If I had to run an extra mile,

00:23:25.771 --> 00:23:27.806
it wouldn't be for classic salted.

00:23:27.806 --> 00:23:30.509
So you know what the next
most-calorific chip is?

00:23:31.576 --> 00:23:33.278
Magic masala, baby.

00:23:33.278 --> 00:23:34.413
Blue Lay's.

00:23:34.413 --> 00:23:35.914
We had to end with this one.

00:23:35.914 --> 00:23:37.048
Super calorific.

00:23:37.048 --> 00:23:39.751
I don't know why I'm
proud of that, but good.

00:23:39.751 --> 00:23:42.654
Great to know that this
is and forever will be

00:23:42.654 --> 00:23:44.723
the maharaja of Lay's.

00:23:44.723 --> 00:23:47.726
In the interest of science,
I will taste this liquid.

00:23:47.726 --> 00:23:48.593
If I do this,

00:23:48.593 --> 00:23:50.996
make sure to subscribe to
the Food Insider channel.

00:23:53.198 --> 00:23:56.802
I never thought you could
drink a fart until today.

00:23:56.802 --> 00:23:58.570
That was quite ...

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:03.241
it was like potato water
with a hint of salt.

